From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 18:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: cix: vpu: replay ACPI top power-on after RCSU reset

The platform bus attaches the generic ACPI PM domain with power_on=true
before calling the AMVX probe.  On Sky1 that evaluates VPU0.PPRS._ON before
the driver has acquired and deasserted vpu_rcsu_reset.  The subsequent
pm_runtime_resume_and_get() normally sees an already-active device and does
not replay the ACPI transition.

Replay the firmware power-resource _ON method after the register-side reset
has been deasserted and before deasserting the VPU reset or touching VPU
MMIO.  Calling acpi_device_set_power(D0) is not sufficient here because the
ACPI core may have cached D0 at platform-domain attach and elide the
method.

Fail runtime resume before VPU MMIO if the firmware method cannot be
evaluated.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
index 80478f672..95d31f60b 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
@@ -1053,6 +1053,26 @@ static void mvx_pdev_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
     mvx_dev_remove(ctx);
 }
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_ACPI
+static int mvx_acpi_power_on(struct device *dev)
+{
+	acpi_handle handle = ACPI_HANDLE(dev);
+	acpi_status status;
+
+	if (!handle)
+		return 0;
+
+	status = acpi_evaluate_object(handle, "PPRS._ON", NULL, NULL);
+	if (ACPI_FAILURE(status)) {
+		dev_err(dev, "failed to replay VPU ACPI power resource _ON: %s\n",
+			acpi_format_exception(status));
+		return -EIO;
+	}
+
+	return 0;
+}
+#endif
 
 static int mvx_hw_init(struct device *dev)
 {
@@ -1211,6 +1230,10 @@ static int mvx_pm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
      */
     if (ctx->rcsu_rstc)
         reset_control_deassert(ctx->rcsu_rstc);
+#ifdef CONFIG_ACPI
+	if (has_acpi_companion(dev) && mvx_acpi_power_on(dev))
+		return -EIO;
+#endif
     reset_control_deassert(ctx->rstc);
     enable_irq(ctx->irq);
 
